## FPGA Integration

The SoC can eventually be synthesized using the FPGA development tools.

The general process is:

    Verilog
      ↓
    Synthesis
      ↓
    Implementation
      ↓
    Bitstream
      ↓
    FPGA
      ↓
    SoC running on hardware

The FPGA board will provide the physical implementation of the SoC.

---

## Important Limitation

This project is not yet the final Linux computer.

The SoC must still have several things completed before Linux can run.

For example:

- A suitable RISC-V CPU
- Correct boot behavior
- Sufficient RAM
- Interrupt support
- Timer support
- UART driver support
- Software toolchain
- Bootloader or firmware
- Linux-compatible hardware configuration
- Device tree
- FPGA hardware verification

This project is therefore the hardware foundation for the Linux stage.

